#: ../../appendix-b-example-codekg/index.md:14 e1f97979672e4b58867fc38f20e5271d
msgid "Appendix B — Example: Build a Code KB From a Go Repository"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-b-example-codekg/index.md:20 6bf9d2ee4a994805a818ead398fe87cb
msgid ""
"This appendix mirrors Appendix A, but for the **code layer**. Where "
"Appendix A turned three Markdown files into a searchable wiki, Appendix B"
" takes the entire `lazy-ai-coder` repository — roughly 19 kLOC of Go plus"
" some Python — and turns it into a queryable code knowledge base: parser "
"→ embeddings → graph → retriever → generator, exactly the pipeline "
"Chapters 8 – 13 built."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-b-example-codekg/index.md:27 efa210e7bdbd4fa9b2b7a06b8af11ac2
msgid ""
"Every command, response body, and latency number below was captured "
"against a single commit of `lazy-ai-coder` (`7afa52003fd6` — the same "
"commit stamped on the Part III excerpt headers by `make book-refresh-"
"excerpts`). Reproduction in any other commit should return "
"*qualitatively* the same answers; only entity counts and wall-clock "
"numbers will drift."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-b-example-codekg/index.md:34 b4b184b457b740af9af5aaaa6b5e853f
msgid "Why"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-b-example-codekg/index.md:36 986d6953ed394499a60aefddbb745a94
